WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>Thanks for making time, Riley, Ken. I'd like to walk through how the pilot went and talk about what the full rollout could look like.</v>

2
00:00:51.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Riley Blake>Sure. Overall the stores have been really positive. Staff picked it up faster than we expected.</v>

3
00:01:31.000 --> 00:02:01.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>Good to hear. On our side, the headline number is attach rate. Across the 50 pilot stores we're seeing a 9% attach-rate lift on smart-home bundles compared with the control stores.</v>

4
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:43.000
<v Riley Blake>That matches what our store managers are telling me. The demo stations especially are pulling people in.</v>

5
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:23.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>So the proposal for next month is to take Aurora to all 400 stores ahead of the holiday season.</v>

6
00:03:48.000 --> 00:04:09.000
<v Riley Blake>That's where I need to be straight with you. We've had Fabrikam Home in as well, and they quoted about 20% under your list price.</v>

7
00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:57.000
<v Riley Blake>If you can get close to that we could sign this quarter. I'd rather stay with Aurora, the pilot has gone well, but price is going to come up.</v>

8
00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:35.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>Understood. Is that 20% on the hub alone, or does it include install and support?</v>

9
00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:09.000
<v Riley Blake>Honestly I'm not sure. I've only seen the per-store number.</v>

10
00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:55.000
<v Riley Blake>And Priya will want the all-in cost. She's joining the pitch, and she'll look at the total for 400 stores, not the sticker price.</v>

11
00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:32.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>That's helpful. I'll bring an all-in, per-store and total view for Priya.</v>

12
00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:27.000
<v Ken Liu>From the IT side, one thing before we go any further. We need a security review before the 400-store rollout. The pilot was a small footprint, so we let it through on a lighter check.</v>

13
00:08:52.000 --> 00:09:14.000
<v Ken Liu>For 400 stores I need to see your security documentation, where the data is stored, and confirm nothing captures customer PII in store.</v>

14
00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:59.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>Absolutely. We have a security and compliance FAQ, and I can set up a session with our team to walk through it with you.</v>

15
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:37.000
<v Ken Liu>That works. As long as it happens before anything is signed for the full rollout.</v>

16
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:27.000
<v Riley Blake>One more thing from the stores: the reconnect issue we saw a couple of times. I'll send details separately, but it's not a blocker for this conversation.</v>

17
00:11:52.000 --> 00:12:12.000
<v Marcus Hollowell>Noted. So next steps: I'll set up the security review with Ken, and I'll come to the pitch with the all-in cost for Priya.</v>

18
00:12:37.000 --> 00:12:45.000
<v Riley Blake>Sounds good. Thanks, Marcus.</v>

19
00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:18.000
<v Ken Liu>Thanks.</v>
